rubrics_metrics.description:
A sequence of marked geodesic balls (B(p_k,s_k), g_k, p_k) (0 < s_k ≤ ∞) with s_k → s (0 < s ≤ ∞) converges in the C^{
locfty} topology to a marked (possibly noncomplete) ball (B(p_∞,s), g_∞, p_∞) if there exist exhausting open sets U_k in B(p_∞,s) and diffeomorphisms f_k: U_k → V_k ⊂ B(p_k,s_k) with f_k(p_∞)=p_k such that the pullback metrics (f_k)^* g_k converge to g_∞ in C^{
locfty} on every compact subset of B(p_∞,s).
